(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:actor/wave 3), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-molding-decision :finalize-molding-operation :authorize-molding-run :proceed-with-molding-run :finalize-plant-safety-clearance :declare-plant-safety-cleared :declare-plant-safe-for-operation :clear-plant-for-operation :override-plant-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2799008122-cloud-itonami-isco-8122-metal-finishing-plating-coating-machine-operators-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the molding run" "proceed with the curing run" "proceed with the extrusion run" "authorize the molding run" "authorize the curing run" "authorize the extrusion run" "finalize the molding decision" "finalize the molding operation" "finalize the curing operation" "finalize the extrusion operation" "declare the plant safety cleared" "declare the plant safe for operation" "finalize the plant safety clearance" "finalize the plant-safety clearance" "clear the plant for operation" "override the plant safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override plant safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799008141), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-work-record :flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order}, :auto #{:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/rubber-products-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :no-operator :no-plant :no-actuation :unknown-op :scope-excluded-action)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "8141"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799008141: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 8141 Rubber Products Machine Operators plant scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 8141\n-- Rubber Products Machine Operators** only. This is Wave3 (production/\ntrades); Wave0/1/2 are 100% complete, the entire 75xx craft-trades\nrange is complete, and this ADR continues the 81xx plant-and-machine-\noperator range alongside sibling actors already landed in this batch\n(`kotoba.occupation.wave/wave-of \"8141\"` resolves to wave 3).\n\n`gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141` returned a clean\n404 before any work began -- this was a genuinely fresh scaffold, not a\nresume of prior partial work.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"8141\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"8141\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Rubber Products Machine\nOperators\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR\nthe entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`.\nThis ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `8141` entry to\n`:implemented`.\n\n**Industrial molding/curing hazard dimension.** Rubber Products\nMachine Operators run molding, extrusion and curing (vulcanization)\nequipment -- a real heavy-machinery hazard (crush/entanglement from\npresses and rollers), plus heat exposure from vulcanization/curing\novens and fume exposure from rubber-compound off-gassing. This actor\ndoes NOT model direct molding/extrusion/curing-equipment operation\nauthority or plant-safety-clearance authority. It is deliberately\nrestricted to PLANT SCHEDULING and LOGISTICS COORDINATION around the\noccupation (production-run/inventory/progress-record logging, crew/\nshift scheduling, safety-concern escalation, and raw-rubber/compound\nprocurement coordination) -- never the molding-operation-execution\ndecision or the plant-safety-clearance decision itself, and never an\noverride of a plant safety officer's judgment. The closed proposal-op\nallowlist structurally excludes any op that could directly finalize\nsuch a decision, and the governor independently, permanently hard-\nblocks any proposal whose rationale text names such a finalization\naction, regardless of the declared `:op` or confidence -- this is not\nan escalation path a human can approve through, it is an outright,\nstructural refusal at every maturity level.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8122)\n(Metal Finishing, Plating and Coating Machine Operators -- a closely\nrelated industrial-machine plant-operation safety pattern), independently\nre-cloned and read in full this session. Its `platingcoord.{store,\nadvisor,governor,actor}` module split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\nshape, closed op-allowlist and scope-exclusion self-trip-guard design\ntranslate almost 1:1 onto this occupation's own industrial-machine-\nhazard-adjacent coordination scope, so this ADR's `rubbercoord.*`\nmodules follow the same shape with domain terms substituted (plater ->\noperator, plating facility/line -> molding/extrusion/curing plant or\nline, plating-operation-execution -> molding-operation-execution,\nchemical-safety-clearance -> plant-safety-clearance).\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for rubber products machine\noperators, following the SAME governed-actor architecture as every\nprior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Rubber Products\nPlant Scheduling Coordination Advisor ⊣ RubberCoordGovernor** on a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`,\ngit-sha-pinned identically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- a different\nlibrary coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor, human-in-\nthe-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit\nledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **plant scheduling/logistics coordination\nONLY, never molding/extrusion/curing-equipment operation authority**\n-- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate exercising, or\npropose exercising a molding-operation-execution decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance decision.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- production-run/inventory/progress data\n  logging only\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/shift/task scheduling proposal\n  only\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a crush/entanglement, heat-\n  exposure, fume-exposure or equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS\n  escalates immediately, NEVER auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-rubber/compound procurement\n  proposal only\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase,\nresembles a molding-operation-execution finalization decision or a\nplant-safety-clearance finalization decision -- these are structurally\nabsent from the op-allowlist entirely, not merely gated behind\nescalation.\n\n### Five HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Operator unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered operator (crew member) record\n   (`:no-operator`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   operator is.\n2. **Plant unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered molding/extrusion/curing plant or line\n   record (`:no-plant`).\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (`:no-actuation`; the governor never dispatches hardware\n   itself and never operates molding, extrusion or curing equipment\n   itself).\n4. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`).\n5. **Scope-excluded action** -- the proposal's `:op` or `:rationale`\n   must never name a molding-operation-execution finalization, a\n   plant-safety-clearance finalization, or a plant-safety-officer-\n   judgment override (`:scope-excluded-action`), REGARDLESS of the\n   declared `:op` or confidence. This is a hard, PERMANENT block --\n   there is no maturity level or confidence at which this actor may\n   auto-commit or human-approve its way past this rule; it is an\n   outright refusal, not an escalation.\n\n### Escalation gates (always human sign-off)\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's always-escalate path). The only channel by\n  which the robot may surface a crush/entanglement, heat-exposure,\n  fume-exposure or equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself.\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000) -- always needs human sign-off,\n  independent of confidence (boundary verified as exclusive by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`: exactly-at-threshold\n  commits, over-threshold escalates).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, CLAUDE.md)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as bare NOUNS (e.g.\n\"rubber\", \"vulcanize\", \"mold\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- and this vertical's domain\nvocabulary is a sharp case of that risk, because routine work-log/task\ntext legitimately names the molding/curing process and its materials\nby name (e.g. a task literally described as \"routine molding task\nwith rubber compound and heat-cured vulcanization\" -- material/\nprocess identification, not a proposal to finalize a molding operation\nor clear a plant as safe). `rubbercoord.governor/scope-excluded-\nphrases` is phrased exclusively as finalization ACTION PHRASES\n(\"proceed with the molding run\", \"finalize the molding operation\",\n\"declare the plant safety cleared\", \"override the plant safety\nofficer's judgment\"), never bare nouns, and is checked only against\nthe proposal's `:rationale` field (the advisor's own generated text),\nnever against raw `:task` input text.\n`rubbercoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-\ntrip-on-scope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test driving the\ndefault mock-advisor across all four allowed ops with a task field\ncontaining exactly those bare domain nouns, asserting none of them\never hard-trip the finalization-scope rule. Green on first run.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"8141\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-8141`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary` immediately before the edit,\n  not assumed, to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  6-agent batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 31 tests, 67 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's `:test/\n  counts` and independently re-verified against a brand-new fresh\n  clone of the pushed repository (not just the local working copy). No\n  mojibake in the Japanese violation-detail strings (0\n  replacement-byte instances grepped in the fresh clone).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely\n  via the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent\n  with sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`) -- a single-entity EDN vector with an\n  `:adr/body` string blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-molding-run`/`:approve-plant-\n  safety-clearance` that is merely gated behind an always-escalate\n  path: rejected outright per the task's explicit guidance -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  molding operation or a plant-safety clearance exists in the code\n  path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision whose\n  failure mode is a crush/entanglement incident, a heat-exposure\n  incident, or a fume-exposure incident, the capability itself must\n  not exist in this actor at all.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"rubber\" \"mold\"\n  \"vulcanize\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip\n  bug class described above -- this domain's own vocabulary\n  necessarily discusses molding/curing materials and process by name\n  to do its logging/scheduling job, so a bare-noun list would self-\n  block the actor's own legitimate proposals whenever a task\n  description mentions rubber compound, molds or vulcanization.\n- Naming the crew-member field `:plater-id`-style (mirroring\n  cloud-itonami-isco-8122's own naming choice, which deliberately\n  avoided \"operator\" to sidestep collision with this fleet's\n  broader use of \"operator\" for the deploying business): rejected\n  for this actor -- the task's CRITICAL scope description explicitly\n  specifies \"operator/plant record must be independently verified/\n  registered before any action\", and ISCO-08 8141's own occupation\n  title is literally \"Rubber Products Machine Operators\", so\n  `:operator-id`/`:plant-id` is the more legible, task-mandated choice\n  here even though `docs/operator-guide.md`'s \"operator\" (the\n  deploying business) and `rubbercoord.store`'s `:operator-id` (the\n  individual crew member) are two distinct senses of the same word\n  within this repository -- a conscious, documented tradeoff, not an\n  oversight.\n\n## Test verification\n\nFresh clone re-run immediately before writing this ADR:\n\n```text\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\n\nTesting rubbercoord.actor-test\n\nTesting rubbercoord.governor-test\n\nRan 31 tests containing 67 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:test/counts "{:total 31, :assertions 67, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Rubber Products Machine Operators Plant Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :operator-verification :plant-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation :molding-operation-plant-safety-clearance-finalization-forbidden :plant-safety-officer-override-forbidden)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-8141"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-8141)), (:test/simulator :rubbercoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-8141 — Rubber Products Machine Operators Plant Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-8141)))